SCP Idea: {Redacted}


23 Dec 2020 03:49






Seeking Greenlights:  Yes

Page Type:  SCP Article

Elevator Pitch:  This SCP is a phenomenon in which nobody can read any information documented about it. You cannot speak of it, cannot read it, cannot hear of it, and cannot see it. Containment procedures (Hints to the entity hidden behind the phenomenon) include an average sized concrete room sealed with two gates and guarded by 3 guards at all times. When entering it's chamber, no less than 4 guards should enter accompanying any other personelle. Cameras are prohibited as they do not work.

Central Narrative:  This SCP came into existence when a scientist attempted to document an anomaly he had discovered, only to realize he couldn't.

Hook/Attention-Grabber:  This SCP is focused around the idea of 'Wait, it's all Redacted? Well then what is it?' Readers can assume their wildest thoughts after reading containment procedures, which allows the reader some info, put not enough to know exactly what it is. Personelle have come up with a general code when discussing the entity, as experiments showed that it can be referred to by a name. Most people of the Site it's contained at know what it is, but the reader doesn't. At the bottom of the article, there could be interviews with people trying to talk about it.

Additional Notes:  All critiques helpful! Something I would like to ask is how would I put this into an article? How do I describe something that cannot be described?





